---
import './modelling.css';
---
<figure class="r01-figure" aria-labelledby="r01-dependencies-title">
  <div class="r01-head"><span>Figure 1</span><p id="r01-dependencies-title">Different facts, different determinants</p></div>
  <div class="r01-dependencies">
    <div class="r01-dependency r01-line-fact">
      <div><strong>One order line</strong><code>(order_id, line_no)</code></div>
      <span class="r01-arrow" aria-label="determines">→</span>
      <div><code>product_id</code><code>quantity</code><code>unit_price</code><small>Which product, how many, at what agreed price?</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="r01-dependency">
      <div><strong>One order</strong><code>order_id</code></div>
      <span class="r01-arrow" aria-label="determines">→</span>
      <div><code>customer_id</code><code>placed_at</code><code>status</code><small>Who placed it, when, and its current status?</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="r01-dependency">
      <div><strong>One customer</strong><code>customer_id</code></div>
      <span class="r01-arrow" aria-label="determines">→</span>
      <div><code>name</code><small>What is this customer called now?</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="r01-dependency">
      <div><strong>One product</strong><code>product_id</code></div>
      <span class="r01-arrow" aria-label="determines">→</span>
      <div><code>name</code><code>price</code><small>Its current catalogue name and price.</small></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Each arrow means that equal values on the left require equal values on the right, within one valid database state. It does not mean the value can never change. The map selects the shop facts needed here; it is not a diagram of storage or query execution.</figcaption>
</figure>
